{"kind":"assert","text":"dap-demo outsider CLI claim (a9c678d0), early Source and evidence assessment by checker session 44e8. Not the final-head review.\n\nPacket /private/tmp/artroom-dap-demo-outsider-review-data-20261023-v1/manifest.json (SHA-256 62fdffed…d237). All 135 copies check: regular file, single link, mode 0444, unique inode, copy hash equal to original hash, exact namespace.\n\nSource, against Main:\n- In walkClaim, commands.ts uses the public creation offer when config.service is the dap-demo origin. It needs real fetch metadata (url and redirected), and the body is cancelled if they are missing. It needs isCurrentCreationOffer for the exact saved register. Every other service keeps the historical member read.\n- The offer only selects the register item. The native found act still decides.\n- wrangler.demo.jsonc records ARTIFACTS_CONFIG with exactly the values in a9c678d0, and demo-config.test.ts pins them.\n\nWitness: outsider-claim.scope.test.ts meets my condition 8793b5e3. It runs the real `dap install` and `dap claim` commands as key sam, who is outside the founders. Every GET of the register summary answers 403 and is counted, and the test requires 0 such reads for both policies. Under open, the claim yields the five sibling pins: directory@16, membership@8, rules@10, destination@12, inbox@1. Under keys, a native found by the same key refuses unauthorized, and the CLI claim exits 1 with no claim and no recovery key kept. A reply without fetch metadata is refused, its body cancelled and never read.\n\nEvidence: the baseline failed at 79:54 (\"same-origin creation offer is unavailable\"), because the test adapter attached url with defineProperty. The test-only correction returns status, body, url and redirected:false, and asserts that the client asked for redirect \"error\". It does not touch the 403 tripwire. That failure stays recorded. The continuation passed. The control set `publicDemo = false` and failed with \"Cannot read sc_…: forbidden\", which is the live failure. Meaningful.\n\nNo required finding.\nP3-1. The dap-demo origin is now written out in four Source places: apps/room/demo-creation.ts, scope demo-creation.ts ORIGIN, Page main.ts and CLI commands.ts. One shared constant would stop them drifting apart.\nP3-2. Limit to state: on the dap-demo service the CLI never reads the member summary. A register other than the configured open one cannot be claimed through the CLI there, even by a founder.\nP3-3. DEMO_START_CONFIG v3 must repeat the DEPLOYMENT value, and part 1's runbook sets DEPLOYMENT as a secret. The part 2 runbook should say how DEMO_START_CONFIG is set: as a secret, or as a plain var that also exposes the DEPLOYMENT value. If it is a --var, every deploy must repeat it, as with ARTIFACTS_CONFIG before."}